		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3664&amp;p=28522#p28522"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I have a friend who bought a V5 MD-9600 and loaded OpenGD77. Works great on FM and DMR Simplex but doesn't work on a DMR Repeater that is a MTR2000 Running Pi-Star on a STM32-DVM-MTR2K board. Any suggestions?</div></blockquote>If you have other radios, confirm that the repeater works with those radios.<br>Check the colour code value and all other settings.<br><br>Check the frequency calibration matches with the radios which can access the repeater.<br><br>Also check other DMR repeaters, if possible.<br><br>AFIK.  MMDVM based DMR repeaters are difficult for the operator to calibrate and small variations in the transmitted modulation and or frequency can prevent them from receiving signals correctly<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Jan 09, 2024 1:55 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
